# Docs naming

Ordinary markdown under `docs/` uses **lowercase + kebab-case**.

```text
✅ docs/file-document-architecture.md
✅ docs/freemind-mm-format-spec.md
❌ docs/FILE_DOCUMENT_ARCHITECTURE.md
❌ docs/Freemind_MM_Format_Spec.md
```

- Prefer short, descriptive slugs (`project-structure-and-build.md`).
- Do not use SCREAMING_SNAKE or Title_Case for new ordinary docs.
- Root files that are repo conventions (`README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `LICENSE`, …) stay as-is; this rule is for `docs/` content.
- When renaming, update all in-repo links and comments that point at the old path.
